  "trademark_checklist": [
    "Search the exact phrase at tmsearch.uspto.gov -> is it LIVE registered in class 25 (apparel) or related? If yes -> avoid.",
    "Is it a brand name, product name, company, or app? -> avoid.",
    "Is it a person's name (celebrity, athlete, influencer, character)? -> avoid (right of publicity + TM).",
    "Is it a team, league, university, or event name/nickname/mascot? -> avoid (licensed).",
    "Is it a 'clever' slogan that could be someone's registered mark (e.g., Mama Bear)? -> verify, default to avoid.",
    "Are we only using generic descriptive words + the customer's own name/credential? -> usually SAFE."
  ],
  "patent_checklist_light": [
    "Utility patent applies to how a physical product FUNCTIONS (a mechanism, closure, construction). A name embroidered on a standard blank sweatshirt/tee = no utility-patent risk.",
    "Design patent protects the ornamental LOOK of a product (e.g., a specific jewelry piece shape, a specific bag design). If copying a distinctive product SHAPE -> risk. Generic blanks -> safe.",
    "For jewelry / physical items: are we copying a specific competitor's unique design, or using a generic/blank form we personalize? Generic + personalization = low risk.",
    "When in doubt on a physical/mechanical product, do a quick Google Patents search of the product type before ordering inventory.",
    "This is a light screen only. Real patent clearance for a physical product = a patent attorney / freedom-to-operate search."
